        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1176">

                <pb facs="1059" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1162</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1914-11-03T13:00:00-05:00" notBefore="1914-11-03T00:00:00+03:25"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Received November 3, 1914, 1 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Russian officers have seized Turkish and Austrian Consuls and archives at Tabriz
                    and sent them to Russia. Germans are threatened and Consul was feloniously
                    assaulted. Paddock has extended temporary refuge and protection to
                    panic-stricken German Consul and subjects. Russians will arrest, expel, and
                    perhaps deport all Germans. Wire instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1176-a1.xml" xpointer="d1176-a1"/>
            </div>
